\i\f0\fs60 Introduction \fs72 1\par
\fs40 The 100% Pure Java\i0\fs20\'99 \i\fs40 Standard\par
\i0\fs20 The \ldblquote 100% Pure Java\f1\'d4 \f0 Standard\rdblquote  is part of Sun Microsystems initiative to\par
promote the development of portable applications, applets, beans, class\par
libraries, and servlets written using the Java\f1\'d4 \f0 Programming language.\par
Compliance to the standard consists of code analysis and testing the program\par
on multiple Java Application Environment.\par
This cookbook will assist you in the process of understanding the guidelines\par
for writing portable code. The steps described in this guide are designed to\par
ensure that your code is portable and that it will meet your customer\rquote s\par
expectations of a 100% Pure Java program.\par
\i\fs40 About this Guide\par
\i0\fs20 This guide covers all of the basic things that you should know about the 100%\par
Pure Java Standard.\par
This document serves as:\par
\bullet  \b Developers Style Guide\b0 : for developers using the Java programming\par
language who want to maximize the portability of their programs. It explains\par
the important difference between merely writing programs using the Java\par
programming language, and writing effective and portable programs that will\par
indeed run on Java Compatible platform or device.\par
\bullet  \b Programming Manual for Purity\b0 : for programmers. It presents the rules for\par
compliance with 100% Pure Java standard. It also provides practical hints and\par
\f2 1 - 2 100% Pure Java Cookbook\par
\cf2\b\fs24 Introduction\par
\cf1\b0\f0\fs20 advice for maximizing portability of programs, and offers workarounds for the\par
most common portability pitfalls encountered when writing software.\par
This document can help you:\par
\bullet  \b Gain purity expertise\b0 : developers can benefit from the collective experience\par
of Sun\rquote s development team. This guide contains information and ideas to help\par
developers achieve the maximum portability with their programs. This guide\par
describes the principles for purity, along with hints for portability.\par
\i\fs32 Contents\par
\i0\fs20 This guide has two purposes: it sets out the rules for achieving the 100% Pure\par
Java standard, and it presents advice and examples to aid the development of\par
fully portable software. It defines the steps you must take to certify a program.\par
It also defines what criteria applies to 100% Pure Java programs and, equally\par
important, what does not.\par
\b\fs24 Chapter 1, "Introduction"\par
\b0\fs20 gives basic definitions that describe the vocabulary of purity. This chapter is\par
important for everyone.\par
\b\fs24 Chapter 2, "Understanding Portability & Purity"\par
\b0\fs20 describes the virtues of purity. The 100% Pure Java standard is not designed\par
for all programs; this chapter will help determine if following the purity\par
standard is appropriate for you.\par
\b\fs24 Chapter 3,"Guidelines for Developing Pure Programs"\par
\b0\fs20 describes the rules and guidelines that a programmer must know in order to\par
develop a 100% Pure Java program.\par
\b\fs24 Chapter 4, "Explanations of Purity Problems and Variances"\par
\b0\fs20 describes the pitfalls that programmers frequently encounter while trying to\par
modify their programs for purity. This chapter will give Sun\rquote s perscribed\par
solutions to these pitfalls. Some pitfalls will require \ldblquote bending\rdblquote  purity rules to\par
some degree.\par
The Appendices also give helpful information describing:\par
\b\fs24 Appendix A, "Available Java Platforms"\par
\b0\fs20 describes the supported architectures, OS types, JAE versions that a pure java\par
program should run on.\par
