\i\fs32 100% Pure Java Definitions\par
\b\i0\fs20 Java Compatible : \b0 A brand that is associated with the JAE. This brand\par
describes that a given version of the Java language compiler, Virtual Machine\par
(VM), and Java Class Libraries (Application Program Interfaces, or API\rquote s) have\par
passed Sun\rquote s conformance tests.\par
\b 100% Pure Java : \b0 A term used to describe programs that follow Sun\rquote s purity\par
standard. This term describes that a program that runs on top of a Java\par
Compatible platform has passed the requirements set forth in this document..\par
\b Java Application Environment (or \lquote JAE\rquote ): \b0 A specific version of the Java\par
language compiler, Virtual Machine (VM), and Java Class Libraries\par
(Application Program Interfaces, or API\rquote s) define the JAE. The Java 2 Platform,\par
Standard Edition is an example of a JAE.\par
\b Java Compatible Platform (or \lquote Platform\rquote ): \b0 A specific combination of computer\par
hardware (or architecture), operating system, and version of a supported JAE.\par
\b Program: \b0 In the context of this document, a program is a self-contained set of\par
classes. A program can be a application, an applet, a class library, a servlet, a\par
bean, or more than one of these.\par
